 "title": "How to Handle an Inappropriate Question",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video provides a simple technique to handle inappropriate or intrusive questions without rushing to answer. The main lesson is to make the person asking explain their motivation, shifting the awkwardness back to them.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not rush to answer an inappropriate question.",
  "Make the person asking explain why they are asking the question.",
  "Example response if someone asks how much money you make: 'Curious, why do you want to know?'",
  "Example response if someone asks why you are single: 'Why is that important to you?'",
  "Let the other person defend their question instead of you defending your answer."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Philipp Humm | Storytelling & Communication Skills. Text / caption: How to Handle an Inappropriate Question. Transcript: And how do we get asked this widely inappropriate question? Watch how she responds. You are in phenomenal shape. Thank you. You're very Well you you're always in great shape. But you had to make sure you were in perfect shape for this one, didn't you? And a particular workout Are you trying to lose weight? Well What's what's the deal, man? You look great. No, no, no. No, seriously, we have to talk about this. What what do you what? Are you trying to fit into a cat suit? This is brilliant. I've trained leaders at companies like Google, JP Morgan and Asics. And this is one of the simplest ways to handle an inappropriate question. Don't rush to answer it. Make them explain why they are asking. Someone ask, hmm, how much money do you make? Curious, why do you want to know? Why are you single? Why is that important to you? And suddenly, the awkwardness goes back to the person who created it. You don't have to defend your answer. Let them defend their question. Try this and follow for more simple tips to speak under pressure. Important text shown on screen: How to Handle an Inappropriate Question",
